    <statement><p>Assume that <m>a</m> and <m>b</m> represent positive real numbers.  Simplify the expression
<me>-5 \sqrt{28 a^{7} b^{2}}</me>
into the simplest radical form <m>A \sqrt{C}</m>, where <m>A</m> and <m>C</m> are either integers or monomials.</p>
<p>Answer: <m>A =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/> and <m>C =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2\cdot \left(-5\right)a^{\frac{7-1}{2}}b^{\frac{2}{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>7a</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
